\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 Ali Yahya, a general partner at a16z Crypto, articulated the firm\u8217 s perspective on privacy in a recent blog post. In a discussion of privacy trends for 2026, Yahya stated that 'privacy will be the most important moat in crypto this year.' This insight underscores the growing consensus among investors and industry leaders that protecting transaction details will be paramount for fostering trust and encouraging broader participation in the blockchain ecosystem.}
