\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 Stitch, a Saudi financial services startup, has secured a $25 million investment from Silicon Valley venture capital firm Andreessen Horowitz. Mohamed Oueida, the Founder and CEO of Stitch, emphasized that this investment is not only significant for their company but for the entire Middle East region. The investment was announced on 17th June 2026, marking a pivotal moment for the startup, as it represents a validation of their business model and ambitions.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 Oueida expressed his enthusiasm about the partnership, stating, "It is a significant investment, and it is a big deal for us, and there\u8217 s no shying away from that. It does represent tremendous validation for us, and our business model. It\u8217 s not just a Stitch story, it\u8217 s a regional one." The CEO highlighted that the funds will primarily be used to accelerate Stitch's growth, allowing the company to expand its operations across the Gulf Cooperation Council (GCC), Egypt, and Southeast Asia, including recent launches in the Philippines.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 The CEO articulated that many financial institutions today are burdened by outdated infrastructure, suggesting that a combination of legacy systems and fragmentation has created inefficiencies. Oueida noted, "Capital isn\u8217 t the problem here; most financial institutions are huge spenders on }
{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b\i\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ul\cf2 technology}{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0
\ulnone\cf2 . However, the ROI they are getting from these investments are not where they should be." He elaborated that many banks are still reliant on legacy systems that hinder their ability to adapt to modern technological advancements, including cloud solutions and artificial intelligence.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 Stitch aims to address these challenges by offering a unified platform to streamline operations and reduce fragmentation. Oueida remarked, "Today, building software is as easy as making food. We believe that you can build a unified platform on a single operating system, rather than having 1,000 systems running, which inevitably leads to high-levels of fragmentation." He also emphasized that AI's true potential cannot be unlocked without addressing the existing fragmentation within financial institutions.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
